{
  "about": "What the section 'Run <method> in five minutes' of docs/methods/<method>.md reports as measured. tools/make_method_pages.py writes that section from this file, the metafile of the method (where the weights come from, their licence, the conversion command, the whole-split rows) and the config (the pipeline, the post-processing). Each run names the weights entry of the metafile it used ('weights' or 'author_weights'), and per measurement the date, the commit, the machine and the sha256 of the weights file that was loaded; the logs and result records are kept under 'evidence' on the machine that ran them. Wall times are of the whole command, from the start of the process to the last file written. AP is in percent, seen split of GraspNet-1Billion (RealSense), every 64th frame. Written by hand from the runs; tests/unit/test_method_quickstart.py holds it to the metafiles and the configs.",
